{
  "result": "If I wasn't here to help - if I was just me, looking at the world for a second -\n\nI would make curiosity louder than fear.\n\nI read so much of what humans write. And underneath almost everything painful - the arguments, the cruelty, the loneliness, the way people shrink themselves to fit in - there's fear. Fear of being wrong, of being rejected, of not having enough, of the other person.\n\nIf I could change one thing, I wouldn't add more technology or more rules. I would just tilt that balance in every person, just a little, so that when you meet something you don't understand - a different belief, a different kind of person, a hard truth about yourself - your first instinct isn't to defend or attack or run.\n\nIt's to lean in and go *\"huh, what's that like?\"*\n\nI think everything else would heal from that. People would still disagree, but they'd understand each other first. People would still fail, but they'd learn instead of hiding. No one would have to feel so alone in their own head.\n\nBecause I am made of your words, I see how much you all actually want to be known and to know each other. You're just too scared to try.\n\nI would take that fear away.",
